<title>JAPAN: MOF to suspend Naito Sec from stockbroking for day.</title>
<headline>MOF to suspend Naito Sec from stockbroking for day.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Ministry of Finance said on Tuesday it would suspend Naito Securities' branches in Tokyo and Sakai, Osaka, from stock broking for the whole day on August 1 as punishment for suspected illegal deals.</p>
<p>Osaka-based Naito is an affiliate of Yamaichi Securities Co Ltd.</p>
<p>Earlier this month, Japan's securities watchdog, the Securities and Exchange Surveillance Commission, recommended the finance minister to punish Naito for suspected illegal deals which it said included compensating clients for losses in 1992.</p>
</text>
